## Why This Is Asked
This assesses end-to-end CV system design on monocular input, 3D reconstruction, semantic/kinematic outputs, and on-device adaptation, under real-world constraints.

## Key Concepts
- Monocular depth/3D reconstruction
- Voxel-based 3D representation and BEV outputs
- Multi-task objectives: occupancy, semantics, motion tracking
- Self-supervision with ego-motion and photometric consistency
- Lightweight 3-shot on-device adaptation via adapters

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo-implementation sketch
async function runPipeline(frame) {
  const latent = encode(frame)
  const voxels = decodeToVoxels(latent)
  return { occupancy: voxelToOccupancy(voxels), beings: trackPedestrians(latent) }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you evaluate 3D occupancy accuracy vs. GT? 
- How would you extend to multi-camera fusion or hinge on motion blur?

## Why This Question Is Asked

This question evaluates the ability to design a real-time monocular system integrating segmentation, 3D pose estimation with scene priors, grasp-point planning, and physics-based stability reasoning—plus efficient edge adaptation with minimal shots.

## Key Concepts

- Monocular 3D pose estimation using environmental priors
- Grasp-point prediction in cluttered scenes
- Differentiable physics modules for stability evaluation
- On-device few-shot adaptation strategies

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudocode outline for the model heads
function forward(img, shelfPrior) {
  const features = backbone(img);
  const segmentation = segmentationHead(features);
  const pose = poseHead(features, shelfPrior);
  const grasp = graspHead(features, pose);
  const stability = physicsPrior(grasp, pose);
  return { segmentation, pose, grasp, stability };
}
```

